From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ppenguin <hieronymusv@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 16:24:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] security(route): loopback needs the gateway service
 credential

Both API groups exempted every request from 127.0.0.1/::1 from the user
token. Loopback is not an identity: any local process, and any container
on the host network, reaches this listener, and this API installs
compose apps (host mounts, privileged containers) as root.

A loopback caller now skips the user token only when it also presents
the gateway's per-start service credential (gateway.token, owner-only;
gatewayclient.ServiceAuthorizationMatches), the credential the gateway's
management API already requires. v1 and v2 share one skipper.

No in-stack service calls this API over loopback today; the dashboard
reaches it through the gateway with a user token.
Stacked on "present the service credential to the message bus" (which
adds the gatewayclient helpers).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
